docs/spec/SPEC.md:202:Keychain service names: `com.usefulbot.opencode-go`, `com.usefulbot.brave`, `com.usefulbot.router.desktop`, `.phone`, `.reviewer`, `.eval`, `.ops` (the latter five expand from `com.usefulbot.router`), `com.usefulbot.channel.desktop` and `.phone` (expand from `com.usefulbot.channel`). Separate values, no shared master bearer. Device tokens and router tokens are 32 random bytes encoded base64url. Configure verifiers with SHA-256 token digests and compare fixed-size digests in constant time. Server-side browser-session tokens are also stored as digests.
docs/spec/SPEC.md:256:Owner runtime configuration supplies the exact tailnet HTTPS origin, phone IPv4 /32 and IPv6 /128 identities and Mac destination identity. Do not put actual values in repository files, documentation or memory. Apply an additive-policy-aware ACL/grant allowing only that phone to the Mac's Serve HTTPS port. Existing broad allow rules must not also grant access. Include policy tests accepting the enrolled phone and denying a second tailnet device, all other Mac services and the router/eve ports. The app additionally verifies the expected owner login identity. VERIFY S4 covers source identity/header behavior for the installed Tailscale version; until it passes, Serve remains disabled.
docs/spec/SPEC.md:297:At turn start, inject <=1,536 units, maximum five notes; reserve at least 512 units for memory-tool results and framing. Root plus reviewer share the same turn's budget ledger. Deduplicate by note ID/revision. Keep the memory envelope after the stable system prefix and mark it untrusted reference data with provenance. New selection replaces the prior memory envelope; do not append another copy every turn. Before compaction, strip old injected envelopes and memory tool text from retained history. A compaction summary must not accumulate a shadow memory store outside this cap. VERIFY memory-history tests inspect all model-visible memory content, not just the latest injection hook.
docs/spec/SPEC.md:341:Search uses Brave's web endpoint `https://api.search.brave.com/res/v1/web/search`, `X-Subscription-Token` supplied only by the router, safe-search strict, no raw result enrichment. [Authentication documentation](https://api-dashboard.search.brave.com/documentation/guides/authentication). POLICY: maximum five results, title 200 characters, snippet 800 characters, HTTPS URL <=2,048 characters; timeout 10 seconds, response body <=1 MiB. Caller limits: desktop 50, phone 10, eval 20 searches per rolling 24h; aggregate 60, at most one/second. Persist counters before dispatch, charge failed/unknown requests conservatively. No automatic retry. Live S5 verifies count/filter parameters against the installed provider API. Search prices/entitlement are VERIFY owner setup; no guessed free tier or paid activation.
