+```
+
+VERIFY generator output naming/flags from the pinned CLI help, then normalize the schema artifact to `spikes/codex/app-server.schema.json` within that later change. Do not read auth files, run `codex doctor` credential output or infer successful auth from catalog flags. The six section 10 assertions are the pass criteria, not merely successful schema generation.
+
+Implementation change management: create a branch before edits, run the appropriate gates, update only stale project markdown, commit with `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:` or `refactor:`, push and open a PR. Run the owner's enabled security/code-review plugins for auth, privilege, credential and SQLite changes. Resolve confirmed high/critical findings and wait for green review before merge. Never force-push, rewrite history, bypass hooks, create an unrequested worktree or commit directly to main. This synthesis makes no implementation commit or claim of passed runtime checks.

